        {
          "id": 583946515,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "There's quite a lot of string preferences that default to \"\" in the dissector. Same thing with the file and directory names. They default to \"\", and if they're not \"\" Wireshark tries to open a file of that name. However, if the user's preferences file sets a value, it's impossible on the command line to set it back to the default.\n\nThe only case of PREF_DIRNAME is in `packet-etch.c` and it defaults to \"\".\n\nI think there's a use case for all of these being allowed to be empty. I think for most of them they default to empty strings in the dissector if not set. All of this is about overriding the user's preferences file. I suppose an alternative would be a \"ignore pref file, use dissector default\" option, or only allowing it for the ones that default to a (which is I think most if not all of them), but that seems more complicated.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
